{{define "optimize"}}
{{$l := .Lang}}{{$a := .Analysis}}{{$lv := .Analysis.Level}}{{$why := .Analysis.LevelWhy}}{{$cr := .Analysis.Crash}}{{$opt := .Analysis.LevelOpt}}{{$ex := .Analysis.Exact}}

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Jadwal di atas kertas versus jadwal yang bisa dijalankan{{else}}The schedule on paper versus the schedule that can be delivered{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    {{if eq $l "id"}}CPM menjawab "sepagi apa pekerjaan ini boleh mulai" dengan satu asumsi diam-diam: sumber daya tak terbatas. Kalau dua aktivitas boleh paralel, CPM menjadwalkannya paralel - tak peduli keduanya membutuhkan satu-satunya Backend Developer di tim. Halaman Organisasi sudah menunjukkan asumsi itu dilanggar pada {{len $a.Resources.Conflicts}} hari-peran. Halaman ini menjawab pertanyaan berikutnya: kalau kapasitas dihormati, kapan proyeknya selesai, dan berapa harga untuk mempercepatnya kembali?{{else}}CPM answers "how early may this work start" under one silent assumption: unlimited resources. If two activities may run in parallel, CPM schedules them in parallel - regardless of whether both need the team's only Backend Developer. The Organisation page already shows that assumption broken on {{len $a.Resources.Conflicts}} role-days. This page answers the next question: if capacity is respected, when does the project finish, and what does it cost to speed it back up?{{end}}
  </p>
  <div class="kpi-grid four">
    <div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">CPM</p><p class="kpi-value">{{$why.CPM}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}hari kerja, kapasitas diabaikan{{else}}working days, capacity ignored{{end}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi bad"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}+ kapasitas nyata{{else}}+ real capacity{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{$why.CapacityOnly}}</p><p class="kpi-note">+{{sub $why.CapacityOnly $why.CPM}} {{if eq $l "id"}}hari dari bentrokan & peran paruh waktu{{else}}days from clashes & half-time roles{{end}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi bad"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}+ periode ujian{{else}}+ exam period{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{$why.WithWindows}}</p><p class="kpi-note">+{{sub $why.WithWindows $why.CapacityOnly}} {{if eq $l "id"}}hari; selesai{{else}}days; finishes{{end}} {{date ($a.FinishISO $lv.Duration) $l}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Peran kritis{{else}}Critical role{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{$a.CriticalRole}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}paling banyak membuat pekerjaan menunggu{{else}}makes work wait the most{{end}}</p></div>
  </div>
  {{if $opt.Proven}}
  <div class="proof">
    <p>{{if eq $l "id"}}<strong>Terbukti optimal.</strong> Tidak ada jadwal yang menghormati kapasitas - dengan urutan apa pun - yang bisa selesai sebelum {{$opt.Bound.Value}} hari kerja, dan jadwal di halaman ini selesai tepat pada {{$lv.Duration}} hari. Versi sebelumnya memakai satu aturan prioritas (LST) yang memberi {{$opt.Baseline.Duration}} hari.{{else}}<strong>Proven optimal.</strong> No schedule that respects capacity - in any order - can finish before {{$opt.Bound.Value}} working days, and the schedule on this page finishes at exactly {{$lv.Duration}} days. The previous version used a single priority rule (LST) that gave {{$opt.Baseline.Duration}} days.{{end}}</p>
  </div>
  {{end}}
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Seberapa dekat dengan jadwal terbaik yang mungkin?{{else}}How close is this to the best possible schedule?{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Penjadwalan berbatas sumber daya adalah masalah NP-hard: tidak ada algoritma cepat yang menjamin jadwal terpendek untuk semua jaringan. Tetapi untuk satu jaringan tertentu, optimalitas bisa DIBUKTIKAN dengan dua angka. Batas atas adalah jadwal nyata terbaik yang berhasil ditemukan. Batas bawah adalah durasi yang secara matematis tidak mungkin dikalahkan. Bila keduanya bertemu, pencarian selesai.{{else}}Resource-constrained scheduling is NP-hard: no fast algorithm guarantees the shortest schedule for every network. But for one specific network, optimality can be PROVEN with two numbers. The upper bound is the best real schedule found. The lower bound is a duration that mathematically cannot be beaten. When the two meet, the search is over.{{end}}</p>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <h3>{{if eq $l "id"}}Batas atas: tiga cara mencari{{else}}Upper bound: three ways to search{{end}}</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="data compact">
        <thead><tr><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Aturan prioritas{{else}}Priority rule{{end}}</th><th class="num">SGS</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}+ justifikasi{{else}}+ justification{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {{range $opt.Rules}}
          <tr><th><code>{{.Rule}}</code> <span class="small muted">{{ruleName .Rule $l}}</span></th><td class="num">{{.Duration}}</td><td class="num">{{.Justified}}</td></tr>
          {{end}}
          <tr class="highlight"><th>{{num (iterf $opt.Samples) 0 $l}} {{if eq $l "id"}}daftar acak berbias{{else}}biased random lists{{end}}</th><td class="num" colspan="2">{{if eq $l "id"}}terbaik{{else}}best{{end}} {{$opt.SampleBest}}, {{if eq $l "id"}}terburuk{{else}}worst{{end}} {{$opt.SampleWorst}}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>
      <p class="small">{{if eq $l "id"}}Keenam aturan klasik terjebak pada jadwal yang sama. Sampel acak berbias - aktivitas mendesak lebih mungkin didahulukan, tetapi tidak selalu - menemukan urutan yang lebih baik: A05 dikerjakan sedikit demi sedikit selama UTS alih-alih menunggu UTS selesai. Justifikasi maju-mundur (menggeser semua aktivitas sekanan mungkin lalu sekiri mungkin) dijalankan pada setiap jadwal, tetapi pada jaringan ini tidak menemukan perbaikan tambahan.{{else}}All six classic rules get stuck on the same schedule. Biased random sampling - urgent activities are more likely, but not certain, to go first - finds a better order: A05 is worked a little at a time during the midterms instead of waiting for them to end. Forward-backward justification (shifting every activity as far right as possible, then as far left) runs on every schedule, but finds no further improvement on this network.{{end}}</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>{{if eq $l "id"}}Batas bawah: tiga lapis argumen{{else}}Lower bound: three layers of argument{{end}}</h3>
      <ul class="dash small">
        <li>{{if eq $l "id"}}<strong>CPM ({{$opt.Bound.CPM}})</strong> - sumber daya tak terbatas.{{else}}<strong>CPM ({{$opt.Bound.CPM}})</strong> - unlimited resources.{{end}}</li>
        <li>{{if eq $l "id"}}<strong>Solo ({{$opt.Bound.Solo}})</strong> - setiap aktivitas dikerjakan sendirian, tetapi pada kapasitas nyata perannya: DevOps paruh waktu, 40% saat ujian, dan aturan laju mulai minimum {{pct (minStartRate) 0 $l}}.{{else}}<strong>Solo ({{$opt.Bound.Solo}})</strong> - every activity worked alone, but at its role's real capacity: half-time DevOps, 40% during exams, and the {{pct (minStartRate) 0 $l}} minimum start rate.{{end}}</li>
        <li>{{if eq $l "id"}}<strong>Energetik ({{$opt.Bound.Energetic}})</strong> - sekelompok aktivitas yang memakai peran sama butuh hari-orang total yang tetap; bila jendela waktu yang mungkin baginya tidak menyediakan kapasitas sebanyak itu, aktivitas sesudahnya harus bergeser. Penalaran ini dirambatkan maju (leluhur) dan mundur (keturunan) sampai titik tetap, lalu tenggat-tenggat yang tersisa diuji secara destruktif.{{else}}<strong>Energetic ({{$opt.Bound.Energetic}})</strong> - a group of activities using the same role needs a fixed total of person-days; if the time window open to them does not supply that much capacity, later activities must shift. The reasoning propagates forward (ancestors) and backward (descendants) to a fixed point, then remaining deadlines are tested destructively.{{end}}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figure class="figure"><div class="figure-body scrollable">{{boundChart $l}}</div></figure>
  <div class="note-box">
    {{$pr := (.Analysis.Final).Proof}}
    <h4>{{if eq $l "id"}}Setiap iterasi simulasi juga dibuktikan optimal{{else}}Every simulation iteration is proven optimal too{{end}}</h4>
    <p>{{if eq $l "id"}}Levelling di dalam simulasi terpadu berjalan bertingkat. Pertama SGS cepat (aturan LST dan urutan jadwal optimal di atas). Lalu batas bawah dihitung untuk durasi acak iterasi itu. Bila keduanya belum bertemu, pencarian lokal memindah satu aktivitas demi satu aktivitas sampai jadwalnya menyentuh batas bawah. Dari {{num (iterf $pr.Iterations) 0 $l}} iterasi: {{num (iterf $pr.ByFastSGS) 0 $l}} sudah optimal dengan SGS cepat, {{num (iterf $pr.BySearch) 0 $l}} terbukti setelah pencarian, dan {{num (iterf $pr.Unproven) 0 $l}} belum terbukti - {{pct $pr.ProvenShare 2 $l}} terbukti optimal. Pencarian menghemat rata-rata {{num $pr.FastGapMean 2 $l}} hari per iterasi (paling banyak {{$pr.FastGapMax}} hari); tanpa itu P80 lapisan kapasitas akan sedikit terlalu pesimistis.{{else}}Levelling inside the integrated simulation runs in tiers. First a fast SGS (the LST rule and the optimal schedule order above). Then a lower bound is computed for that iteration's random durations. If the two do not meet, local search moves one activity at a time until the schedule touches the lower bound. Of {{num (iterf $pr.Iterations) 0 $l}} iterations: {{num (iterf $pr.ByFastSGS) 0 $l}} are already optimal with the fast SGS, {{num (iterf $pr.BySearch) 0 $l}} are proven after search, and {{num (iterf $pr.Unproven) 0 $l}} remain unproven - {{pct $pr.ProvenShare 2 $l}} proven optimal. Search saves {{num $pr.FastGapMean 2 $l}} days per iteration on average (at most {{$pr.FastGapMax}} days); without it the capacity layer's P80 would be slightly too pessimistic.{{end}}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Kalender ketersediaan tim{{else}}Team availability calendar{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Risiko R08 pada register menyebut anggota tim tidak tersedia saat ujian kampus. Di sini risiko itu berhenti menjadi kalimat dan menjadi kapasitas yang dihitung. Seluruh tanggal UTS dan UAS dibaca dari lampiran kalender akademik resmi Universitas Esa Unggul TA 2025/2026. Faktor kapasitas {{pct (examFactor) 0 $l}} adalah asumsi perencanaan - halaman Prakiraan Berjalan mengujinya terhadap realisasi selama UTS. Karena R08 sudah dimodelkan sebagai jendela ketersediaan, dampak jadwalnya tidak dihitung ulang di simulasi terpadu.{{else}}Risk R08 in the register says team members are unavailable during campus exams. Here that risk stops being a sentence and becomes computed capacity. Every midterm and final exam date is read from the appendix of the official Universitas Esa Unggul 2025/2026 academic calendar. The {{pct (examFactor) 0 $l}} capacity factor is a planning assumption - the In-flight Forecast page tests it against actuals during the midterms. Because R08 is modelled as an availability window, its schedule impact is not counted again in the integrated simulation.{{end}}</p>
  <table class="data">
    <thead><tr><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Periode{{else}}Period{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Keterangan{{else}}Description{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Kapasitas tersisa{{else}}Remaining capacity{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Peran{{else}}Roles{{end}}</th><th>{{t $l "t.status"}}</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range availability}}
      <tr>
        <td class="small">{{date .From $l}} – {{date .To $l}}</td>
        <td>{{tx .Label $l}} <span class="muted small">({{if eq $l "id"}}memodelkan{{else}}models{{end}} {{.RiskID}})</span></td>
        <td class="num">{{pct .Factor 0 $l}}</td>
        <td class="small">{{if eq (len .Roles) 10}}{{if eq $l "id"}}seluruh tim{{else}}whole team{{end}}{{else}}{{range $i, $r := .Roles}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$r}}{{end}}{{end}}</td>
        <td>{{if .Asumsi}}<span class="pill warn">{{if eq $l "id"}}tanggal asumsi{{else}}assumed dates{{end}}</span>{{else}}<span class="pill ok">{{if eq $l "id"}}tanggal resmi{{else}}official dates{{end}}</span> <a class="source-link" href="{{.Source}}" rel="noopener">{{if eq $l "id"}}sumber{{else}}source{{end}}</a>{{end}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{end}}
      <tr>
        <td class="small">{{if eq $l "id"}}sepanjang proyek{{else}}whole project{{end}}</td>
        <td>{{if eq $l "id"}}DevOps Engineer ditandai opsional pada Project Charter - dimodelkan paruh waktu{{else}}DevOps Engineer is marked optional in the Project Charter - modelled as half-time{{end}}</td>
        <td class="num">50%</td><td class="small">OPS</td>
        <td><span class="pill ok">{{if eq $l "id"}}dari piagam{{else}}from charter{{end}}</span></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Gantt: CPM dibanding levelling{{else}}Gantt: CPM versus levelled{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Batang tipis transparan adalah jadwal CPM. Batang padat adalah jadwal setelah levelling, diwarnai menurut penyebab pergeserannya. Arahkan kursor ke batang untuk melihat berapa hari terbawa dari pendahulu, berapa hari menunggu orang, dan berapa hari memanjang saat dikerjakan.{{else}}The thin translucent bar is the CPM schedule. The solid bar is the schedule after levelling, coloured by what moved it. Hover a bar to see how many days were carried from predecessors, how many were spent waiting for people, and how many the work stretched while in progress.{{end}}</p>
  <figure class="figure">
    <div class="figure-body scrollable wide">{{ganttLevelled $l}}</div>
    <figcaption class="below">
      <p class="legend">
        <span class="swatch ghost"></span> CPM
        <span class="swatch cause-carried"></span> {{if eq $l "id"}}terbawa pendahulu{{else}}carried from predecessor{{end}}
        <span class="swatch cause-shared"></span> {{if eq $l "id"}}menunggu / berbagi orang{{else}}waiting / sharing a person{{end}}
        <span class="swatch cause-halftime"></span> {{if eq $l "id"}}peran paruh waktu{{else}}half-time role{{end}}
        <span class="swatch cause-window"></span> {{if eq $l "id"}}melewati periode ujian{{else}}crosses the exam period{{end}}
      </p>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Pembebanan setelah levelling{{else}}Loading after levelling{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Histogram yang sama dengan halaman Organisasi, kini untuk jadwal levelling. Tidak ada satu batang pun yang melewati garis kapasitas - itulah syarat jadwal yang bisa dijalankan. Perhatikan garis kapasitas yang turun pada periode ujian.{{else}}The same histogram as the Organisation page, now for the levelled schedule. Not a single bar crosses the capacity line - that is what makes a schedule deliverable. Note how the capacity line drops during the exam period.{{end}}</p>
  <figure class="figure">
    <div class="figure-body scrollable wide">{{levelHistogram $l}}</div>
  </figure>
  <div class="two-col">
    <table class="data">
      <caption>{{if eq $l "id"}}Hari menunggu sumber daya, per peran dominan{{else}}Days waiting for resources, by dominant role{{end}}</caption>
      <thead><tr><th>{{t $l "t.role"}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Hari menunggu{{else}}Days waiting{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range $a.SortedRoleWait}}
        <tr class="{{if eq .Role $a.CriticalRole}}highlight{{end}}"><th>{{.Role}}</th><td class="num">{{.Days}}</td></tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <div class="note-box warn">
      <h4>{{if eq $l "id"}}Satu orang menjadi leher botol{{else}}One person becomes the bottleneck{{end}}</h4>
      <p>{{if eq $l "id"}}Backend Developer harus mengerjakan A16, A17, A18, dan A19 - total {{sumDur "A16" "A17" "A18" "A19"}} hari kerja - dan CPM mengira dua di antaranya bisa paralel. Jadwal optimal mendahulukan jalur kritis (A17→A18), sehingga A19 menunggu {{(levelTask "A19").WaitDays}} hari{{if (levelTask "A19").Window}} lalu tertabrak periode ujian{{end}}. Kebetulan, peran ini diisi Daniel Hutajulu dalam dokumen tugas.{{else}}The Backend Developer must deliver A16, A17, A18, and A19 - {{sumDur "A16" "A17" "A18" "A19"}} working days in all - and CPM assumed two of them could overlap. The optimal schedule puts the critical path (A17→A18) first, so A19 waits {{(levelTask "A19").WaitDays}} days{{if (levelTask "A19").Window}} and then runs into the exam period{{end}}. As it happens, this is the role Daniel Hutajulu holds in the assignment documents.{{end}}</p>
      <p><strong>{{t $l "t.recommend"}}:</strong> {{if eq $l "id"}}Pindahkan A19 (API panel admin) ke Technical Lead atau tambah satu backend paruh waktu selama fase pengembangan. Karena jadwal ini sudah terbukti optimal, mengubah urutan tidak akan membantu - hanya menambah kapasitas pada peran yang menjadi leher botol.{{else}}Move A19 (admin panel API) to the Technical Lead, or add a part-time backend developer during development. Because this schedule is already proven optimal, reordering will not help - only adding capacity to the bottleneck role will.{{end}}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Aktivitas yang bergeser{{else}}Activities that moved{{end}}</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data sticky">
      <thead><tr><th>{{t $l "t.code"}}</th><th>{{t $l "t.activity"}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Selesai CPM{{else}}CPM finish{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Selesai levelling{{else}}Levelled finish{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Geser{{else}}Shift{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Terbawa{{else}}Carried{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Menunggu{{else}}Waiting{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Memanjang{{else}}Stretch{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Penyebab{{else}}Cause{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {{$acts := activityByID}}
        {{range $a.MovedTasks}}
        {{$act := index $acts .ID}}
        <tr>
          <td><code>{{.ID}}</code></td>
          <td>{{tx $act.Name $l}}</td>
          <td class="small num">{{dateShort (dateAt (sub (add .ES .Duration) 1)) $l}}</td>
          <td class="small num">{{dateShort (dateAt (sub .Finish 1)) $l}}</td>
          <td class="num neg">+{{.Delay}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{.CarriedDays}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{.WaitDays}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{.StretchDays}}</td>
          <td class="small">
            {{if .HalfTime}}<span class="pill bad">{{if eq $l "id"}}paruh waktu{{else}}half-time{{end}}</span>{{end}}
            {{if .Window}}<span class="pill warn">{{if eq $l "id"}}ujian{{else}}exams{{end}}</span>{{end}}
            {{if .Shared}}<span class="pill neutral">{{if eq $l "id"}}berbagi orang{{else}}shared person{{end}}</span>{{end}}
            {{if and (gt (f .CarriedDays) 0.0) (not .HalfTime) (not .Window) (not .Shared) (eq .WaitDays 0)}}<span class="pill neutral">{{if eq $l "id"}}terbawa{{else}}carried{{end}}</span>{{end}}
          </td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Crashing: membeli waktu dengan uang{{else}}Crashing: buying time with money{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Modul 4 menyebut kompresi jadwal sebagai cara mempersingkat proyek tanpa mengubah lingkup. Crashing menambah sumber daya - lembur, tambahan orang - pada aktivitas kritis yang paling murah dipercepat. Kurva di bawah dihitung dua kali: dengan algoritma serakah (setiap langkah memotong satu hari termurah dan tidak pernah membatalkan potongan lama), dan secara eksak dengan pemrograman linear. Keduanya dibandingkan titik demi titik.{{else}}Module 4 describes schedule compression as shortening a project without changing scope. Crashing adds resources - overtime, extra people - to the critical activities that are cheapest to accelerate. The curve below is computed twice: with a greedy algorithm (each step cuts the cheapest single day and never undoes an earlier cut), and exactly with linear programming. The two are compared point by point.{{end}}</p>
  <div class="kpi-grid four">
    <div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Durasi minimum{{else}}Minimum duration{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{$cr.MinDuration}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}dari{{else}}from{{end}} {{$cr.NormalDuration}} {{t $l "t.days"}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}5 hari pertama{{else}}First 5 days{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{rpShort (index $cr.Steps 4).TotalCost $l}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}premi; bersih setelah sewa{{else}}premium; net of rentals{{end}} {{rpShort (netCrash 5) $l}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi bad"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Kompresi penuh{{else}}Full compression{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{rpShort (index $cr.Steps (sub (len $cr.Steps) 1)).TotalCost $l}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{len $cr.Steps}} {{if eq $l "id"}}hari dipotong{{else}}days cut{{end}}</p></div>
    {{$pr := crashPremiumRange}}<div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Premi lembur{{else}}Overtime premium{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{pct (index $pr 0) 0 $l}}–{{pct (index $pr 1) 1 $l}}</p><p class="kpi-note"><a href="{{overtimeURL}}" rel="noopener">PP 35/2021</a>; {{illegalCrashCount}} {{if eq $l "id"}}aktivitas melebihi batas 4 jam{{else}}activities exceed the 4-hour limit{{end}}</p></div>
  </div>
  <figure class="figure">
    <div class="figure-body scrollable">{{crashCurve $l}}</div>
    <figcaption class="below"><p class="small">{{if eq $l "id"}}Titik jingga menandai langkah yang harus memotong lebih dari satu aktivitas sekaligus karena ada jalur kritis paralel.{{else}}Orange points mark steps that must cut more than one activity at once because of parallel critical paths.{{end}}</p></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data sticky">
      <thead><tr><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Durasi{{else}}Duration{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Dipotong{{else}}Cut{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Biaya langkah{{else}}Step cost{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Kumulatif{{else}}Cumulative{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Simpul kritis{{else}}Critical nodes{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range $cr.Steps}}
        <tr class="{{if gt (f (len .Crashed)) 1.0}}highlight{{end}}">
          <td class="num">{{.Duration}}</td>
          <td>{{range $i, $c := .Crashed}}{{if $i}} + {{end}}<code>{{$c}}</code>{{end}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{rp .StepCost $l}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{rp .TotalCost $l}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{.CriticalAt}}</td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">{{tx $cr.Exhausted $l}}</p>

  <h3>{{if eq $l "id"}}Crashing eksak dan biaya total{{else}}Exact crashing and total cost{{end}}</h3>
  <p class="section-intro small">{{if eq $l "id"}}Untuk setiap tenggat T, LP meminimalkan jumlah biaya marjinal hari-hari yang dipotong - hari kedua dari aktivitas yang sama lebih mahal dari hari pertama - dengan batasan setiap relasi FS dan setiap aktivitas selesai paling lambat T. Matriks batasannya unimodular total, sehingga solusi simpleks selalu berupa hari bulat dan langsung bisa dijalankan - setiap solusi tetap diperiksa ulang dengan CPM. Versi kedua menambahkan biaya sewa server dan langganan tools ({{rp $a.RentalDaily $l}} per hari setelah semuanya berjalan): memendekkan proyek juga memendekkan tagihan.{{else}}For each deadline T, the LP minimises the sum of the marginal costs of the days cut - the second day from the same activity costs more than the first - subject to every FS relation and every activity finishing by T. The constraint matrix is totally unimodular, so the simplex solution is always whole days and directly executable - each solution is still re-checked with CPM. The second version adds server rental and tool subscriptions ({{rp $a.RentalDaily $l}} per day once all are running): shortening the project also shortens the bill.{{end}}</p>
  <div class="kpi-grid four">
    <div class="kpi {{if $ex.GreedyOptimal}}good{{else}}bad{{end}}"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Serakah vs eksak{{else}}Greedy vs exact{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{if $ex.GreedyOptimal}}={{else}}+{{rp $ex.MaxGreedyExcess $l}}{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if $ex.GreedyOptimal}}{{if eq $l "id"}}serakah optimal di setiap titik{{else}}greedy is optimal at every point{{end}}{{else}}{{if eq $l "id"}}kelebihan terbesar serakah{{else}}largest greedy excess{{end}}{{end}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Durasi minimum eksak{{else}}Exact minimum duration{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{$ex.ExactMin}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}serakah{{else}}greedy{{end}} {{$cr.MinDuration}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi good"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Biaya total terendah{{else}}Lowest total cost{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{$ex.Optimum.Duration}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{t $l "t.days"}}; {{rpShort $ex.Optimum.Total $l}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Bersih 5 hari pertama{{else}}Net first 5 days{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{rpShort (netCrash 5) $l}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}premi{{else}}premium{{end}} {{rpShort (exactAt (sub $ex.Normal 5)).CrashCost $l}}</p></div>
  </div>
  <figure class="figure">
    <div class="figure-body scrollable">{{tradeOffChart $l}}</div>
    <figcaption class="below"><p class="small">{{if eq $l "id"}}Titik jingga adalah biaya serakah yang lebih mahal dari optimum eksak. Titik hijau adalah durasi dengan biaya total terendah.{{else}}Orange points are greedy costs above the exact optimum. The green point is the duration with the lowest total cost.{{end}}</p></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data sticky compact">
      <thead><tr><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Durasi{{else}}Duration{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Serakah{{else}}Greedy{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Eksak (LP){{else}}Exact (LP){{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Potongan eksak{{else}}Exact cuts{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Sewa{{else}}Rentals{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Biaya total{{else}}Total cost{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range $ex.Points}}
        <tr class="{{if gt .Greedy (addf .CrashCost 0.5)}}highlight{{end}}">
          <td class="num">{{.Duration}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{if lt .Greedy 0.0}}—{{else}}{{rp .Greedy $l}}{{end}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{rp .CrashCost $l}}</td>
          <td class="small">{{cutsText .Cuts}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{rp .Rental $l}}</td>
          <td class="num"><strong>{{rp .Total $l}}</strong></td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>{{if eq $l "id"}}Lembur pada jadwal yang bisa dijalankan{{else}}Overtime on the executable schedule{{end}}</h3>
  {{$ot := $a.Overtime}}
  <p class="section-intro small">{{if eq $l "id"}}Kurva di atas memotong jaringan CPM {{$a.Plan.Duration}} hari, yang tidak menghormati kapasitas orang. Pada jadwal levelling {{$ot.Levelled}} hari, lembur tidak memendekkan isi pekerjaan - lembur menambah jam kerja: untuk pekerjaan lain yang menunggu, dan untuk mempercepat pekerjaan orang itu sendiri sampai {{num (addf 1.0 (div $ot.HoursPerDay 8.0)) 2 $l}} hari kerja per hari. Jam di atas alokasi rencana dihitung dan dibayar sebagai lembur. Batasnya {{num $ot.HoursPerDay 1 $l}} jam sehari, supaya lembur setiap hari kerja tetap di bawah 18 jam seminggu (<a href="{{overtimeURL}}" rel="noopener">PP 35/2021</a> Pasal 26). Lembur hanya untuk peran penuh waktu{{if $ot.Excluded}} ({{range $i, $r := $ot.Excluded}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$r}}{{end}} paruh waktu tidak diberi lembur){{end}}, dan tidak pada periode ujian: tim yang sedang ujian tidak menjadi lebih tersedia karena dibayar lembur.{{else}}The curve above cuts the {{$a.Plan.Duration}}-day CPM network, which ignores people's capacity. On the {{$ot.Levelled}}-day levelled schedule, overtime does not shorten the work content - it adds working hours: for other waiting work, and to speed up that person's own task up to {{num (addf 1.0 (div $ot.HoursPerDay 8.0)) 2 $l}} working days per day. Hours above the planned allocation are counted and paid as overtime. The limit is {{num $ot.HoursPerDay 1 $l}} hours a day, so overtime on every working day stays under 18 hours a week (<a href="{{overtimeURL}}" rel="noopener">Government Regulation 35/2021</a> Art. 26). Only full-time roles work overtime{{if $ot.Excluded}} (part-time {{range $i, $r := $ot.Excluded}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$r}}{{end}} gets none){{end}}, and never during exam periods: a team sitting exams does not become more available because overtime is paid.{{end}}</p>
  {{if $ot.Points}}{{$minp := index $ot.Points (sub (len $ot.Points) 1)}}{{$days := sub $ot.Levelled $ot.MinDuration}}
  <div class="kpi-grid four">
    <div class="kpi {{if $ot.MinProven}}good{{else}}warn{{end}}"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Durasi minimum dengan lembur{{else}}Minimum duration with overtime{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{$ot.MinDuration}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}batas bawah{{else}}lower bound{{end}} {{$ot.Bound.Value}}{{if $ot.MinProven}} - {{if eq $l "id"}}terbukti{{else}}proven{{end}}{{end}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Hari yang bisa dibeli{{else}}Days that can be bought{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{$days}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}dari{{else}}from{{end}} {{$ot.Levelled}} {{t $l "t.days"}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi bad"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Upah lembur{{else}}Overtime pay{{end}} {{$days}} {{t $l "t.days"}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{rpShort $minp.Cost $l}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}bersih{{else}}net{{end}} {{rpShort $minp.Net $l}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Crashing CPM, hari sama{{else}}CPM crashing, same days{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{rpShort (exactAt (sub $ex.Normal $days)).CrashCost $l}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}hanya sah di atas kertas{{else}}valid only on paper{{end}}</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data compact">
      <thead><tr><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Durasi{{else}}Duration{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Selesai{{else}}Finish{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Lembur per peran{{else}}Overtime by role{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Hari-peran lembur{{else}}Overtime role-days{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Maks/minggu{{else}}Max/week{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Upah lembur{{else}}Overtime pay{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Sewa dihemat{{else}}Rentals saved{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Bersih{{else}}Net{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="num">{{$ot.Levelled}}</td><td>{{date ($a.FinishISO $ot.Levelled) $l}}</td><td class="small">{{if eq $l "id"}}tanpa lembur{{else}}no overtime{{end}}</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">—</td><td class="num">{{rp 0.0 $l}}</td><td class="num">—</td><td class="num">{{rp 0.0 $l}}</td></tr>
        {{range $ot.Points}}
        <tr class="{{if eq .Duration $ot.MinDuration}}highlight{{end}}">
          <td class="num">{{.Duration}}</td>
          <td>{{date ($a.FinishISO .Duration) $l}}</td>
          <td class="small">{{$a.OvertimeRoleText . $l}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{$a.OvertimeDays .}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{num .MaxWeek 1 $l}} {{if eq $l "id"}}jam{{else}}h{{end}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{rp .Cost $l}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{rp .RentalSaved $l}}</td>
          <td class="num"><strong>{{rp .Net $l}}</strong></td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">{{if eq $l "id"}}Durasi minimum {{$ot.MinDuration}} hari {{if $ot.MinProven}}terbukti: batas bawah energetik pada kapasitas lembur maksimum juga {{$ot.Bound.Value}}, dan setiap rencana lembur sah memakai kapasitas yang tidak lebih besar{{else}}belum terbukti: batas bawah pada kapasitas lembur maksimum {{$ot.Bound.Value}}{{end}}. Upah per durasi adalah rencana termurah yang ditemukan dengan memangkas lembur yang tidak diperlukan - batas atas biaya minimum, bukan minimum yang terbukti.{{else}}The minimum of {{$ot.MinDuration}} days is {{if $ot.MinProven}}proven: the energetic lower bound at maximum overtime capacity is also {{$ot.Bound.Value}}, and every legal overtime plan uses no more capacity{{else}}not proven: the lower bound at maximum overtime capacity is {{$ot.Bound.Value}}{{end}}. The pay per duration is the cheapest plan found by trimming overtime that is not needed - an upper bound on the minimum cost, not a proven minimum.{{end}}</p>
  {{if $a.Decision}}{{if $a.Decision.PlanMissed}}<p class="small"><strong>{{if eq $l "id"}}Rencana ini dihitung dari hari pertama proyek dan tidak bisa dibeli lagi:{{else}}This plan is computed from the project's first day and can no longer be bought:{{end}}</strong> {{if eq $l "id"}}{{$a.Decision.PlanMissed}} hari-peran lemburnya jatuh sebelum tanggal data. Opsi yang masih tersedia ada di{{else}}{{$a.Decision.PlanMissed}} of its overtime role-days fall before the data date. The options still available are on{{end}} <a href="{{.BaseURL}}{{pathFor "/keputusan/" $l}}">{{t $l "nav.decision"}}</a>.</p>{{end}}{{end}}
  {{else}}
  <p class="small">{{if eq $l "id"}}Lembur sah tidak memendekkan jadwal ini sama sekali.{{else}}Legal overtime does not shorten this schedule at all.{{end}}</p>
  {{end}}

  <h3>{{if eq $l "id"}}Batas crash per aktivitas{{else}}Crash limits per activity{{end}}</h3>
  <p class="section-intro small">{{if eq $l "id"}}Satu aturan untuk semua, supaya tidak ada angka yang dipilih-pilih: durasi crash = max(O, M − max(1, ⌊M/3⌋)), biaya memotong k hari = upah harian × k × premi lembur(k). Premi tidak diasumsikan: pekerjaan hari yang dipotong dibagi rata sebagai jam lembur ke hari yang tersisa, lalu dibayar menurut <a href="{{overtimeURL}}" rel="noopener">PP 35/2021</a> - jam pertama 1,5×, jam berikutnya 2× upah sejam, paling lama 4 jam sehari. Karena jam kedua dan seterusnya dibayar 2×, hari kedua yang dipotong dari aktivitas yang sama lebih mahal dari hari pertama. Empat aktivitas tidak bisa dipercepat dengan uang, dan {{illegalCrashCount}} aktivitas dua hari tidak boleh dipotong karena butuh 8 jam lembur dalam sehari.{{else}}One rule for all, so no figure is hand-picked: crash duration = max(O, M − max(1, ⌊M/3⌋)), cost of cutting k days = daily wage × k × overtime premium(k). The premium is not assumed: the cut day's work is spread as overtime over the remaining days and paid under <a href="{{overtimeURL}}" rel="noopener">Government Regulation 35/2021</a> - first hour 1.5×, later hours 2× the hourly wage, at most 4 hours a day. Because the second and later hours are paid 2×, the second day cut from the same activity costs more than the first. Four activities cannot be accelerated with money, and {{illegalCrashCount}} two-day activities may not be cut because they would need 8 overtime hours in a day.{{end}}</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data compact">
      <thead><tr><th>{{t $l "t.code"}}</th><th>{{t $l "t.activity"}}</th><th class="num">M</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Crash{{else}}Crash{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Lembur/hari{{else}}Overtime/day{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Premi per hari dipotong{{else}}Premium per day cut{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Biaya per hari dipotong{{else}}Cost per day cut{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Catatan{{else}}Note{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range activities}}
        {{if not .Milestone}}
        {{$cp := crashPlanOf .}}
        <tr class="{{if isCritical .ID}}is-critical{{end}}">
          <td><code>{{.ID}}</code></td>
          <td>{{tx .Name $l}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{.Duration}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{if $cp.Allowed}}{{$cp.CrashDur}}{{else}}—{{end}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{if $cp.Allowed}}{{num $cp.OvertimeHrs 2 $l}} {{if eq $l "id"}}jam{{else}}h{{end}}{{else}}—{{end}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{if $cp.Allowed}}{{range $i, $m := $cp.MarginalPremium}}{{if $i}} → {{end}}{{pct $m 1 $l}}{{end}}{{else}}—{{end}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{if $cp.Allowed}}{{range $i, $m := $cp.Marginal}}{{if $i}} → {{end}}{{rp $m $l}}{{end}}{{else}}—{{end}}</td>
          <td class="small">{{if not $cp.Allowed}}{{tx $cp.Reason $l}}{{end}}</td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Fast-tracking: membeli waktu dengan risiko{{else}}Fast-tracking: buying time with risk{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Fast-tracking menjalankan pekerjaan yang semula berurutan secara tumpang tindih: penerus dimulai saat pendahulunya baru setengah jalan. Tidak ada uang yang keluar di muka, tetapi sebagian pekerjaan dikerjakan di atas masukan yang belum final dan harus diulang. Setiap relasi FS di jalur kritis diuji sebagai kandidat dengan tumpang tindih 50%, lalu CPM dihitung ulang.{{else}}Fast-tracking runs sequential work in overlap: the successor starts while its predecessor is only half done. No money is spent up front, but part of the work is built on inputs that are not yet final and must be redone. Every FS relation on the critical path is tested as a candidate with 50% overlap, then CPM is recomputed.{{end}}</p>
  <div class="note-box warn">
    <p>{{if eq $l "id"}}<strong>Kandidat yang dikerjakan orang yang sama ditolak.</strong> A16→A17 dan A17→A18 tampak menghemat 3 hari masing-masing di CPM, tetapi ketiganya dikerjakan satu Backend Developer. Satu orang tidak bisa mengerjakan dua pekerjaan tumpang tindih; penghematan itu hanya ilusi yang akan hilang begitu levelling dijalankan.{{else}}<strong>Candidates done by the same person are rejected.</strong> A16→A17 and A17→A18 appear to save 3 days each under CPM, but all three are done by one Backend Developer. One person cannot do two overlapping jobs; that saving is an illusion that vanishes the moment levelling runs.{{end}}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data sticky">
      <thead><tr><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Pendahulu → Penerus{{else}}Predecessor → Successor{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Tumpang tindih{{else}}Overlap{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Hemat{{else}}Saves{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Rework harapan{{else}}Expected rework{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Per hari hemat{{else}}Per day saved{{end}}</th><th>{{t $l "t.status"}}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range $a.FastTracks}}
        <tr class="{{if not .Viable}}muted{{end}}">
          <td><code>{{.Pred}}</code> → <code>{{.Succ}}</code></td>
          <td class="num">{{.OverlapDays}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{.DaysSaved}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{rp .ExpectedRework $l}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{if gt (f .DaysSaved) 0.0}}{{rp .CostPerDay $l}}{{else}}—{{end}}</td>
          <td>{{if .Viable}}<span class="pill ok">{{if eq $l "id"}}layak{{else}}viable{{end}}</span>{{else if .SameResource}}<span class="pill bad">{{if eq $l "id"}}orang yang sama{{else}}same person{{end}}</span>{{else}}<span class="pill neutral">{{if eq $l "id"}}tidak memendekkan{{else}}does not shorten{{end}}</span>{{end}}</td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="note-box">
    <h4>{{if eq $l "id"}}Penghematan tidak bisa dijumlahkan{{else}}Savings do not add up{{end}}</h4>
    <p>{{if eq $l "id"}}Ada {{len $a.FastViable}} kandidat layak. Menjumlahkan penghematannya satu per satu memberi angka yang menggoda, tetapi menerapkan semuanya sekaligus hanya memendekkan proyek dari {{$a.Plan.Duration}} menjadi {{$a.FastAllDur}} hari kerja: memendekkan satu jalur membuat jalur lain menjadi kritis. Peluang rework yang diasumsikan {{pct (reworkProb) 0 $l}}.{{else}}There are {{len $a.FastViable}} viable candidates. Adding their savings one by one gives a tempting figure, but applying all of them at once only shortens the project from {{$a.Plan.Duration}} to {{$a.FastAllDur}} working days: shortening one path makes another critical. The assumed rework probability is {{pct (reworkProb) 0 $l}}.{{end}}</p>
    <p><strong>{{t $l "t.recommend"}}:</strong> {{if eq $l "id"}}Crashing lebih cocok untuk proyek ini daripada fast-tracking. Cadangan kontinjensinya sudah hanya menutup {{pct $a.Risk.ReserveCoverage 0 $l}} paparan risiko; menambah risiko rework di atasnya memperbesar lubang yang sama. Crashing lima hari pertama menelan premi {{rp (index $cr.Steps 4).TotalCost $l}}, tetapi setelah sewa yang dihemat dihitung, biaya bersihnya hanya {{rp (netCrash 5) $l}} - biaya pasti yang nyaris impas dan layak diajukan ke sponsor.{{else}}Crashing suits this project better than fast-tracking. Its contingency reserve already covers only {{pct $a.Risk.ReserveCoverage 0 $l}} of risk exposure; adding rework risk on top widens the same hole. Crashing the first five days costs {{rp (index $cr.Steps 4).TotalCost $l}} in premiums, but once saved rentals are counted the net cost is only {{rp (netCrash 5) $l}} - a known, near break-even cost worth putting to the sponsor.{{end}}</p>
  </div>
</section>
{{end}}
